 ('years_confessed', 'status', "the years confessed — the STATUS the answer writes on Jacob: 'how many are the days of the years of your life? ... the days of the years of my sojournings are a hundred and thirty years; few and evil have been the days of the years of my life, and they have not reached the days of the years of the life of my fathers' (47:8-9) — the marker's number; Megillah 17a:4's arithmetic; the run 'few and evil' at its one seat (measured)",
  H(47, 9, 'מעט ורעים היו ימי שני חיי', 'few and evil have been the days of the years of my life'), "Gen 47:8-9 (a hundred and thirty, parsed — the descent's marker), 47:28; %s Megillah 17a:4" % BT, C((47, 8), (47, 9)), X + ' (goshen)'),
 ('holding_given', 'transfer', "a holding given — the TRANSFER the settling writes to the sons: 'and Joseph settled his father and his brothers, and gave them a holding in the land of Egypt, in the best of the land, in the land of Rameses, as Pharaoh had commanded' (47:11) — CLOSES goshen_promised and good_of_egypt_promised; the run 'the land of Rameses' at its one seat (measured; Exodus 1:11 and 12:37 name the city)",
  H(47, 11, 'ויתן להם אחזה בארץ מצרים במיטב הארץ בארץ רעמסס', 'and gave them a holding in the land of Egypt, in the best of the land, in the land of Rameses'), "Gen 47:11, 47:6, 45:18, 47:27 ('and they took holding in it'); Exod 1:11, 12:37 (the exodus story's Rameses)", C((47, 11)), X + ' (goshen)'),
 ('sustained_by_the_mouth', 'status', "sustained by the mouth of the little ones — the STATUS the provision writes on the house of Jacob: 'and Joseph sustained his father, and his brothers, and all his father\'s house, with bread, by the mouth of the little ones' (47:12) — CLOSES sustenance_promised; Nazir 3a:6's 'sustain'; the run at its one seat (measured)",
  H(47, 12, 'ויכלכל יוסף את אביו ואת אחיו ואת כל בית אביו לחם לפי הטף', 'and Joseph sustained his father, and his brothers, and all his father\'s house, with bread, by the mouth of the little ones'), "Gen 47:12, 45:11, 50:21; %s Nazir 3a:6" % BT, C((47, 12)), X + ' (goshen)'),
 # ---- Gen 47 (the_fifth) ----
 ('silver_gathered_to_pharaoh', 'transfer', "the silver gathered to Pharaoh — the TRANSFER the famine's first year writes from Egypt to Pharaoh: 'and Joseph gleaned all the silver found in the land of Egypt and in the land of Canaan for the grain which they were buying, and Joseph brought the silver into Pharaoh\'s house' (47:14) — Pesachim 119a:6",
  H(47, 14, 'ויבא יוסף את הכסף ביתה פרעה', 'and Joseph brought the silver into Pharaoh\'s house'), "Gen 47:13-15 ('the silver is spent' — the run 'the silver is gone' at 47:15 and 47:16, measured); %s Pesachim 119a:6" % BT, C((47, 13), (47, 14), (47, 15)), X + ' (the_fifth)'),
 ('livestock_to_pharaoh', 'transfer', "the livestock to Pharaoh — the TRANSFER the second exchange writes: 'give your livestock, and I will give you for your livestock, if the silver is gone' (47:16), 'and Joseph gave them bread for the horses, and for the livestock of the flocks, and for the livestock of the herds, and for the donkeys, and he led them with bread for all their livestock in that year' (47:17)",
  H(47, 17, 'וינהלם בלחם בכל מקנהם בשנה ההוא', 'and he led them with bread for all their livestock in that year'), "Gen 47:16-17", C((47, 16), (47, 17)), X + ' (the_fifth)'),
 ('bodies_and_ground_offered', 'status', "bodies and ground offered — the STATUS the second year writes on Egypt: 'and that year ended, and they came to him the second year and said: we will not hide from my lord that the silver is spent, and the livestock is my lord\'s; there is nothing left before my lord but our bodies and our ground' (47:18), 'buy us and our ground for bread, and we with our ground will be servants to Pharaoh; and give seed' (47:19)",
  H(47, 18, 'לא נשאר לפני אדני בלתי אם גויתנו ואדמתנו', 'there is nothing left before my lord but our bodies and our ground'), "Gen 47:18-19", C((47, 18), (47, 19)), X + ' (the_fifth)'),
 ('ground_of_egypt_acquired', 'transfer', "the ground of Egypt acquired — the TRANSFER the purchase writes to Pharaoh: 'and Joseph bought all the ground of Egypt for Pharaoh, for Egypt sold every man his field, for the famine was strong upon them; and the land became Pharaoh\'s' (47:20) — the family engine's purchased kind at Joseph's seat, its own effect field_acquired the family's (23:16, 33:19)",
  H(47, 20, 'ויקן יוסף את כל אדמת מצרים לפרעה', 'and Joseph bought all the ground of Egypt for Pharaoh'), "Gen 47:20, 47:23 ('I have bought you this day and your ground for Pharaoh' — the run at its one seat, measured), 47:26", C((47, 20)), X + ' (the_fifth)'),
 ('people_moved_to_cities', 'status', "the people moved to the cities — the STATUS the resettlement writes on Egypt: 'and the people, he moved them to the cities, from one end of the border of Egypt to its other end' (47:21) — Chullin 60b:15: to remove the shame from his brothers, that they not be called exiles",
  H(47, 21, 'ואת העם העביר אתו לערים', 'and the people, he moved them to the cities'), "Gen 47:21; %s Chullin 60b:15" % BT, C((47, 21)), X + ' (the_fifth)'),
 ('priests_ground_exempt', 'status', "the priests' ground exempt — the STATUS the exception writes on the priests of Egypt: 'only the ground of the priests he did not buy, for the priests had a statute-portion from Pharaoh, and they ate their statute-portion which Pharaoh gave them; therefore they did not sell their ground' (47:22), repeated at 47:26 — Beitzah 16a:3: the token means sustenance; the priesthood engine's 'statute' a homograph (FALSE)",
  H(47, 22, 'רק אדמת הכהנים לא קנה כי חק לכהנים מאת פרעה', 'only the ground of the priests he did not buy, for the priests had a statute-portion from Pharaoh'), "Gen 47:22, 47:26 (the token's two Genesis seats, measured); %s Beitzah 16a:3" % BT, C((47, 22)), X + ' (the_fifth)'),
